    'Joe Smith signed a one-year, $1.75 million deal far below his value, with a secret promise of a much bigger contract once Minnesota held his Bird rights. McHale later said many teams did the same, just better hidden. An agent dispute exposed the papers, and the league fined the Wolves $3.5 million, took five years of first-round picks, voided Smith\'s contracts and suspended owner Glen Taylor. Garnett\'s next window was gone before it opened. That May, his close friend and teammate Malik Sealy was killed by a drunk driver.',
