    'In February 2012 Jeremy Lin, an undrafted point guard who had been stuck on the bench, started a seven-game Knicks winning streak, averaging 22.5 points and 8.1 assists, with 38 against the Lakers. "Linsanity" sold out the Garden and pushed ticket prices up as much as 50%. It was over that July, when Lin signed with Houston through the poison pill provision.',
