    'Detroit drafts a reluctant Isiah Thomas',
    'Detroit was coming off a 21-61 season when general manager Jack McCloskey took Isiah Thomas second overall in 1981, just after Thomas led Indiana to the NCAA title, even though Thomas was reluctant to join the franchise at first. McCloskey kept building around him, trading for Bill Laimbeer in 1982 and taking Joe Dumars 18th in 1985, and under Chuck Daly the Pistons became contenders.',
